<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $K'$ be a $\kappa $-small simplicial set, and $p': K' \rightarrow \calC _{p/}$ a $\kappa $-small diagram. Then we may identify $p'$ with a map $q: K \star K' \rightarrow \calC $, and we get an isomorphism $( \calC _{p/} )_{p'/} \simeq \calC _{q/}$. Since $K \star K'$ is $\kappa $-small, the $\infty $-category $\calC _{q/}$ is nonempty. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>